Week 1 Progress Report
Data Acquisition & BI Foundations
Scope
Week 1 covers building the scraping infrastructure for the secondary electronics market and standing up the BI
layer's foundation, including importing the internal manufacturing datasets that Week 2 onward will join against.
Data Engineering — Scraping Infrastructure
Built a spider targeting the secondary electronics market, with two implementations sharing one output schema:
• Production spider (scrapy_project/spiders/secondary_market_spider.py) — a real Scrapy spider. Obeys
robots.txt, throttles requests (DOWNLOAD_DELAY = 1.0s), identifies itself with a custom User-Agent, and
exports to a JSON-lines feed.
• Local runnable version (fallback_scraper.py) — identical extraction logic, used to validate the pipeline in
an environment without Scrapy or live internet access. Same input, same output schema — a drop-in swap
once Scrapy is available.
Source data: a mock secondary-market site (220 listings) generated to reflect real-world messiness — mixed
whole-laptop and spare-part listings, inconsistent title formatting, marketing noise ("L@@K", "FAST SHIP"), and
varied condition labels.
Result: 220 / 220 listings successfully crawled and extracted to the Bronze layer with zero parse failures.

